     "id": "notes-1",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "t": "prose",
       "md": "The model behind [Random Effects Demeaning Weight](note:random-effects-demeaning-weight). Place that view, not this note."
      },
      {
       "t": "prose",
       "md": "- **Model.** [Random Effects Model](note:random-effects-model): GLS subtracts $\\alpha$ times each unit's means, $\\alpha = 1 - \\sigma_e/\\sqrt{T\\sigma_u^2 + \\sigma_e^2}$; $\\rho = \\sigma_u^2/(\\sigma_u^2 + \\sigma_e^2)$.\n- **Tests.** Python: the wage panel ($\\hat\\sigma_u^2 = 0.1083$, $\\hat\\sigma_e = 0.1951$) gives $\\alpha = 0.7437$ at $T = 5$, 0.4900 at $T = 1$, 0.8686 at $T = 20$; $\\rho = 0.7399$."
      }
     ],
     "words": 38,
